        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "In this research, we used a deep learning method focused on Fusion CNN architecture to derive facial patches and depth of 3 types of human facial image samples namely Color, Depth and IR from the CASIA-SURF dataset modeled with an altered 3D convolutional neural network classifier. Our primary interest was to be able to extract facial patches and the depth levels of all 3 facial inputs stated earlier on to distinguish a real face from a spoofed face from a CASIA-SURF dataset provided which are not preprocessed.",
          "block_bbox": [
